OL,3,GNEWSACarer told woman she could leave
OL,4,Awhen dead
OL,5,
OL,6,FA worker at a care home told a resident
OL,7,Fwho repeatedly asked to go home that
OL,8,Fshe would leave when she died,
OL,9,Faccording to an inspection report.
OL,11,FIt was one example of staff speaking to
OL,12,Fpeople in a derogatory way at Saxon
OL,13,FLodge in Canterbury, which has been
OL,14,Fplaced in special measures after
OL,15,Finspectors found a series of failings,
OL,16,Fthe Care Quality Commission (CQC) said.
OL,18,FThe report, published on Thursday, said
OL,19,Fmedicines were not managed safely, food
OL,20,Fwas not in line with people's
OL,21,Frequirements and people who were
OL,22,Fdistressed were not kept safe.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
